Math for Trades, Volume 2 — Flinn and Overgaard (@ql-source-trades-2: 0, is #book, #part-of @ql-sources) { r_1ZNA6BX80YPB0DAYSAED5F6E9X
Chad Flinn and Mark Overgaard. Math for Trades: Volume 2. BCcampus, 2021. English. Ebook ISBN 978-1-77420-113-8.

[Publisher's complete book and downloads](https://opentextbc.ca/mathfortrades2/) · [Contents](https://opentextbc.ca/mathfortrades2/table-of-contents/). CC BY 4.0, except separately credited components. Credit authors, title, BCcampus, year, and source; preserve image-specific notices.

Read all four parts: Understanding and Working with Units; Working with Equations; Perimeter and Area; Volume. Work the practice quizzes and final test. Revisit chapters 1–5 for conversions, 7–9 for formulas, 11–12 for plane geometry, and 14–16 for solid geometry. Chapter numbers here follow this BCcampus web edition.

Keep the difference between mass and force explicit while reading trade expressions such as weight. A familiar gallon or pressure unit needs an exact definition before conversion. The linked book supports the common practical foundation; dimensional reasoning and the SI reference extend it.

The landing page supplies authorized PDF and EPUB downloads. No copy is bundled here. Access, chapter titles, and licence checked on 28 October 2026.

